# Security headers for the whole agnusdei.ai deployment (site/ at the
# root, the demo under /bede/ — see scripts/build_pages_site.sh). Read by
# Cloudflare's Workers Static Assets the same way it reads a Pages
# project's _headers file: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/
#
# Mirrors, as closely as a static file allows, the header set the actual
# product already enforces at two layers — homeschool-api/core/middleware.py's
# SecurityHeadersMiddleware and homeschool-tutor/nginx.conf — so the public
# marketing/demo surface isn't held to a lower bar than the self-hosted app
# itself. See docs/SECURITY.md.
#
# Rule precedence: Cloudflare applies the MOST SPECIFIC matching path's
# value for a given header name, so /bede/*'s block below overrides the
# general /* block for the two headers where the demo genuinely needs a
# different policy (microphone access, and its own API origin) — every
# other header applies identically everywhere.
#
# Deliberately does NOT set Cache-Control (unlike the two reference
# implementations above, which both send no-store — correct for dynamic,
# per-request API/app responses). This is static, publicly-cacheable
# marketing/demo content with no per-visitor data in the response body,
# so an explicit no-store here would only make the site slower to no
# security benefit; Cloudflare's own default asset caching applies.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), microphone=()
  X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; media-src 'self'; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self';

# The interactive demo needs two exceptions the plain marketing pages
# don't: microphone access (press-and-hold voice input), and permission to
# reach its own backend on Render. That backend's exact subdomain is set
# per-deployment by the VITE_DEMO_API_BASE build variable (see
# docs/DEMO_HOSTING.md), not a fixed value this repo can pin — scoped to
# https://*.onrender.com rather than opened up broadly.
/bede/*
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), microphone=(self)
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.onrender.com; media-src 'self' blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self';
